    "lawCode": "Add §§220-i & 231-a, Lab L; amd §70, Pub Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Labor Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7846\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the labor law and the public service law, in relation to\nestablishing requirements for the transfer, sale, lease and any decom-\nmissioning activities of the Indian Point Nuclear Power Plant\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill seeks to protect the rights and privileges of the employees of\nthe Indian Point Nuclear Power Plant\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 requires that all employees of the Indian Point Nuclear Power\nPlant be paid a wage no less than the prevailing wage in the locality\nwhere the Indian Point Nuclear Power Plant is located. In addition, this\nsection states that no part of it can diminish the rights, privileges,\nor remedies of any current or former employee under any other law or\nregulation, collective bargaining agreement, or employment contract.\n\nSection 2 requires that anyone with a contract to purchase or involved\nin the transfer, lease, or decommissioning the Indian Point Nuclear\nPower Plant must pay employees of the Indian Point Nuclear Power Plant a\nwage no less than the prevailing wage of the locality it is located. In\naddition, this section states that no part of it can diminish the\nrights, privileges, or remedies of any current or former employee under\nany other law or regulation or under any collective bargaining agreement\nor employment contract.\n\nSection 3 prohibits the commission to give consent to transfer, lease,\nor sell any franchise, works, system, stock, or bonds of a nuclear power\nplant that is within sixty miles of a city with a population of one\nmillion or more unless certain standards are met. Firstly, the transfer-\nee or purchaser maintains the current workforce through the conclusion\nof the transfer, lease, or purchase. In hiring new employees, the trans-\nferee or purchaser must also hire from a pool of current employees which\nmeet the required skills and to the extent that is practicable. The\ntransferee or purchaser must also enter into and maintain a labor peace\nagreement with a bona fide labor organization which represents the\nemployees of the nuclear power plant. Lastly, the purchaser or transfer-\nee must comply with all applicable labor laws, including but not limited\nto article twenty-five-A of the labor law.\n\nSection 4 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation seeks to limit the damage caused by the imminent\nclosure of the Indian Point Nuclear Power Plant. The bill does so by\nensuring that the employees of Indian Point maintain their positions for\nas long as is feasible, with their prevailing wage in effect.  Corpo-\nrations, firms, companies, partnerships, LLCs and associations with\ncontracts to purchase Indian Point will be expected to maintain the\ncurrent workforce to the extent practical, and new hires will be\nselected from a list of qualified employees of the power plant.\n\nResidents and employees affected by the closing of the Indian Point\nNuclear Power Plant are facing the loss of jobs. Moreover, the dangers\ninvolved in decommissioning a nuclear power plant are best handled by a\nskilled workforce that is familiar with the environment.  Accordingly,\nthis legislation not only protects jobs, but protects the safety and\nsecurity of Indian Point throughout its closure.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law, while section three of the act shall take effect imme-\ndiately after it becomes law.\n",
